      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "6. A: Zhèibān chē yǒu cānchē ba?     This train has a dining car, I\n                                       suppose?\n   B: Yǒu. Yǒu Zhōngcān, yě yǒu      Yes. There's Chinese food and\n      Xīcān.                          there's also Western food.\n   A: Hǎojíle.                        Great.\n\nNote on No. 6\n\nThe ending -jíle, meaning \"extremely,\" \"awfully,\" may be added to adjectival verbs.\n\nNèige píngguǒ dàjíle.            That apple is huge.\nZuò huǒchē fāngbianjíle.         Riding the train is extremely\n                                 convenient.\nTā zǒude kuàijíle.               He walks awfully fast.\n\n-jíle is seldom used in Taiwan.\n"
